From: backslashxx/KernelSU contributors
Subject: [PATCH 04/04] reboot: hook sys_reboot for supercall (KSU, 3.18+)

Insert ksu_handle_sys_reboot() at the top of sys_reboot().
Needed for KernelSU supercall (introduced at v12143). 3.18+ variant
matches 4.14 (sys_reboot lives in kernel/reboot.c with this signature).

Guard with `#ifndef CONFIG_KSU_KPROBES_KSUD` so we don't double-hook when
kprobes are available.

Reference: backslashxx/KernelSU Issue #5 (v2.3, "3.18+").
---
 kernel/reboot.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kernel/reboot.c b/kernel/reboot.c
--- a/kernel/reboot.c
+++ b/kernel/reboot.c
@@ -282,6 +282,12 @@ SYSCALL_DEFINE4(reboot, int, magic1, int, magic2, unsigned int, cmd,
 		void __user *, arg)
 {
 	struct pid_namespace *pid_ns = task_active_pid_ns(current);
 	char buffer[256];
 	int ret = 0;
+
+#if defined(CONFIG_KSU) && !defined(CONFIG_KSU_KPROBES_KSUD)
+	extern int ksu_handle_sys_reboot(int, int, unsigned int, void __user **);
+	ksu_handle_sys_reboot(magic1, magic2, cmd, &arg);
+#endif
 
 	/* We only trust the superuser with rebooting the system. */
 	if (!ns_capable(pid_ns->user_ns, CAP_SYS_BOOT))
--
2.34.1